const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server running on port ${PORT}`);
});
```

You can now run `node server.js` in production, while your test suite can simply require `app` and attach a supertest agent without the server auto‑starting.

