## 6️⃣ Content‑Security‑Policy (CSP) & Other Headers

Helmet already sets a decent CSP, but you can tighten it further:

```js
app.use(
  helmet.contentSecurityPolicy({
    directives: {
      defaultSrc: ["'self'"],
      scriptSrc: ["'self'"], // no inline scripts
      styleSrc: ["'self'", 'https://fonts.googleapis.com'],
      imgSrc: ["'self'", 'data:'],
      connectSrc: ["'self'"],
      fontSrc: ["'self'", 'https://fonts.gstatic.com'],
    },
  })
);
```

If you later serve static assets, use `express.static` with proper cache‑control:

```js
app.use(
  '/public',
  express.static('public', {
    maxAge: '1d',
    setHeaders: (res, path) => {
      if (path.endsWith('.html')) {
        // No caching for HTML (helps with security updates)
        res.setHeader('Cache-Control', 'no-store');
      }
    },
  })
);
```

